    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the membership level rules with the new points system.\n\n**New behavior** \u2014 points start at 0, then: +2 for an email, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, +2 for a household of 3+, +3 for tenure over 365 days; level maps as 1 (0-1), 2 (2-3), 3 (4-5), 4 (6+). Both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel` are returned.\n\n**Changes, kept structurally small:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains its setter) and updated `membershipLevel` (max now 4, new description).\n- **`MembershipPoints.java`** (new) \u2014 one small static method scoring the four factors, with the `Tenure` helper carried over.\n- **`MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 rewritten into a trivial points\u2192level mapping (`of(int membershipPoints)`), replacing the old direct-factor logic.\n- **`RespondWithOwner.java`** / **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 each swaps its single `setMembershipLevel(...)` line for computing the points once, setting both fields.\n\nEach changed function is a single-method unit with essentially no surrounding class complexity, so the biggest cost lever (WMC_other) stays at its floor. The new scoring logic lives in its own cohesive class rather than growing an existing one.",
