    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as defined in `owners.POST.yml` and its function classes. Every step runs under a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`) that commits once at the very end.\n\n## 0. Authorization (gate, before any step)\n`composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` \u2014 caller lacking the role is rejected (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## 1. `BuildOwner`\n- **Validation** \u2014 requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` to be non-null/non-blank; any missing ones are collected and thrown as `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 maps the request DTO to an `Owner`; sets `registrationDate` to `nextBusinessDay(...)` of the supplied date (or today if absent), i.e. a Saturday/Sunday is rolled forward to Monday.\n\n## 2. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`\n- **Validation** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is after `nextBusinessDay(today)`, throw `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**. (Same-day or absent is accepted; the comparison rolls \"today\" the same way.)\n\n## 3. `ValidateOwnerPostcode`\n- **Validation** \u2014 postcode is optional; when present it must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in that range. Otherwise `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"postcode\")` \u2192 **400**. Absent postcode is left untouched.\n\n## 4. `NormalizeOwnerAddress`\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 rewrites `address` in place: trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`.\n- **Validation** \u2014 if the address is blank after trimming \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"address\")` \u2192 **400**.\n\n## 5. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 rewrites `telephone` in place into E.164 form (strips spaces/dashes/brackets; assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0` when no `+`).\n- **Validation** \u2014 if it cannot form valid E.164 (length / country-code-length rules) \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")` \u2192 **400**.\n\n## 6. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`\n- Email is optional; a null/blank value is left untouched.\n- **Validation** \u2014 if present, must match the email pattern, else **400**; and the domain must not be disposable (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), else **400**.\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 lower-cases `email` in place.\n\n## 7. `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`\n- **Validation** \u2014 scans all owners; if another owner shares this owner's identity (normalized **telephone AND email** both equal) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## 8. `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold`\n- **Validation** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold == true` (which bypasses), if another owner has the same `HouseholdId` (same normalized **last name + postcode**) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## 9. `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`\n- **Validation** \u2014 if the owner's city (trimmed, case-insensitive) already holds **\u2265 50** existing owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## 10. `RejectOwnerDailyLimit`\n- **Validation** \u2014 if **\u2265 100** owners already share this owner's `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n## 11. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 sets `customerCode` to `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from postcode/city locality and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n## 12. `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 persists via `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; writes an AUDIT log line (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`).\n\n## 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effects (response decoration)** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and computes/attaches:\n  - `namesakeCount` (other owners with same first+last name),\n  - `membershipPoints` (email present +2, no namesakes +1, household \u22653 +2, tenure >365 days +3),\n  - `membershipLevel` (1\u20134 banding of points),\n  - `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 other owners share the registration date),\n  - `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` (same last name + postcode but different telephone; null when `sharesHousehold`).\n- Responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Then** the surrounding transaction commits (once, covering all steps).\n\nA note on ordering rationale baked into the pipeline: presence validation happens first (step 1) so missing fields are a 400 before anything else; the future-date and postcode checks precede the normalizers; all duplicate/capacity/limit rejections run **before** `customerCode` assignment and `save`, so a rejected request commits nothing."
